# Invocation the sibling golden PNG was captured with (#3849).
# Regenerate both together: BYROREDUX_REGEN_GOLDEN=1 cargo test --release \
#   -p byroredux -- --ignored cube_demo_golden_frame
#
# THIS BASELINE IS STALE — deliberately recorded as captured, not as wanted.
#
# cube_demo_60f.png was last regenerated by 4376f7a6 on 2026-06-04 (#1320).
# That run predates BOTH flags the test passes today:
#   * --bench-mode renderer-static  — added to the harness by f19f7f15 on
#     2026-08-11, ten weeks after the capture. Before it, dt was not fixed at
#     zero, so the stored frame comes from a different timing regime.
#   * --upscaler taa                — added by #3849. FSR3 landed 2026-07-22
#     and parse_args defaults --upscaler to fsr3, so between then and now the
#     test rendered through the FidelityFX chain at reduced internal
#     resolution while the baseline is a native-TAA frame.
# 550 renderer commits (272 touching shaders) have landed since the capture.
#
# The staleness gate therefore fires on the first run and says so, instead of
# letting the pixel compare report 100 % baseline drift as a renderer
# regression. Regenerating needs a Vulkan device and a release build, and it
# OVERWRITES the committed PNG — so it is left to a human at the machine.
frames=60
